{"contract":"rgp-pems2-admission-transaction/2","expected_base_sha256":"5b51892902b6949a5bf23daa201974cfee797de99e15601d755ff6d446e1d5c4","new_records":[{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Reasoning Graph Protocol Engineer directive defines RGP as domain-independent and assigns generic protocol, validator, evaluation, pressure-case, and framework work without project-specific canonical authority."},"id":"pems:proposition:092753f85a335f184608bb93","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:594b76dea4743d5cb6c90691"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The invocation-request schema requires an explicit project root, non-empty evidence and source registry, invocation identity/time, and output paths under reasoning-distiller-invocation/1."},"id":"pems:proposition:09a798ffff084d128ce0df36","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:8efc4629f21bee176c629fab"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The RGP output schema permits only observation, decision, assumption, uncertainty, and claim records; only supports, contradicts, depends_on, and supersedes relations; and requires primary provenance for non-derived observations."},"id":"pems:proposition:0fd5aa5ce2ab3b9c62e89510","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:07b2cf9cb2cdd15a7b01e5a2"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The package-build configuration allowlists admission, agents, backends, protocols, runtime, schemas, and validators as managed release roots while excluding CI, docs, evaluation, project knowledge, and tests from the installed package."},"id":"pems:proposition:1b7fb780ddb0f6ad1bcbcd74","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:291809737cc49197defbbbdd"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The release-package builder validates the source tree, collects only configured managed files, constructs a canonical manifest/content identity, builds deterministic tar.gz bytes, and verifies the resulting archive."},"id":"pems:proposition:286145105faa1fe88b0e3815","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:8670843fcfbcae2b62a2adb5"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The PEMS/RGP compatibility fixture set distinguishes lossless exportable domain records from states that cannot be represented losslessly in RGP/1."},"id":"pems:proposition:390cde03ac0cfa46e485bd8a","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:3ce6ab5129f500e2e72ea8aa"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Distiller directive treats source identifiers as opaque, prohibits inferring source authority from identifier spelling, and prefers omission over invented provenance or semantic repair."},"id":"pems:proposition:3b93d9deebf59c5061f2cdcf","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:77729cc15cb2cf00f6b275b7"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The package validator computes content identity from semantic manifest content, validates safe relative paths and managed-root containment, and separately validates package manifests and installation records against schemas."},"id":"pems:proposition:3cc5e4e2e43e9df995f92023","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:46e00ade6563ae7a9e2d29ba"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The legacy distillation validator provides deterministic structural validation of Reasoning Distiller graph output using the same closed record/relation and provenance concepts."},"id":"pems:proposition:3eb929b8aed32e1b18f7037b","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:893979427e545395dfeb965d"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The PEMS admission fixture set includes cases for canonical identity reuse, distinct identity under domain refinement, atomic derived-subgraph admission, and other reconciliation/admission pressure conditions."},"id":"pems:proposition:4f7612dd8fdf3e53d6c31418","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:6ede58ec6cbe26f66eb0f4cf"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The install-package manifest schema binds version, source commit, content identity, transport SHA-256, compatibility, managed roots, and exact file entries under reasoning-distiller-install-package/1."},"id":"pems:proposition:54432109dbb68d1ee9ae7f83","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:af2a38b7b5b560153cf33a1a"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The RGP uncertainty-import fixtures map RGP/1 uncertainty to current PEMS unresolved_item records with open resolution state rather than silently converting uncertainty into a proposition claim."},"id":"pems:proposition:7175345f7a7e876f2183d24f","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:aa6723bac686784470cfefd8"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Steward directive explicitly states that the generic role contract does not grant authority by itself."},"id":"pems:proposition:74c07806d79862c01cc8e087","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:ae29b365fc8dbf7615b205c7"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The PEMS/2 validator performs deterministic structural, compatibility, migration, admission-pressure, graph-integrity, and candidate-document checks without mutating canonical memory."},"id":"pems:proposition:7a0f7b651e955dc7907e03ce","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:905e374b54b18bf87e0cc3e8"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The PEMS/2 schema requires semantic, project_id, records, and relations and describes graph integrity, identity admission, provenance semantics, deterministic normalization, and retention as semantic validation responsibilities beyond JSON Schema."},"id":"pems:proposition:86ead7291e53af5040753bac","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:8904c4ebd752b8b04ea87fc6"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The RGP Submission Protocol does not grant canonical admission, alter RGP semantics, select a canonical backend, or transfer ownership of project knowledge."},"id":"pems:proposition:9acfb3c3ad73c9ebed87b03b","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:e11e43caf4c8e733b85ea32a"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The installer is a deterministic network-independent local installer that verifies release identity, archive shape, managed drift, project compatibility, transition state, and installed-tree validity before/after mutation."},"id":"pems:proposition:9b1c99f823b4a9953573f05c","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:77e8bcea1214c5d4003b8939"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The v1 admission executor applies a Steward-authorized admission plan only to an exact PEMS/2 snapshot and includes deterministic PEMS normalization, graph-integrity validation, and COVE encoding/round-trip logic."},"id":"pems:proposition:9eeb1c6fcfa79f7a07832f12","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:35a4a36f1d5ca4d77df8b1ed"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Project Knowledge Package schema defines project identity, compatible framework contracts, project-owned locations, and optional canonical backend configuration as consuming-project configuration."},"id":"pems:proposition:ac8e15618e076bbcd5a980f2","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:59e5eb37b331de657ff32b7f"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The package-build configuration ignores generated Python cache artifacts and applies a deterministic default file-mode policy."},"id":"pems:proposition:b70192052b72cb8aa0b1e6ac","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:291809737cc49197defbbbdd"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The RGP Submission Protocol defines immutable candidate submission and immutable Steward disposition as a generic handoff and keeps candidate production, semantic reconciliation, admission, and canonical persistence distinct."},"id":"pems:proposition:bcd4e8b565d6334b417e6745","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:e11e43caf4c8e733b85ea32a"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The installer uses a durable project-local transaction journal to recover interrupted installation and update operations and exposes recovery separately from transition planning."},"id":"pems:proposition:bfd097abe7a2e3217eb4cf4f","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:77e8bcea1214c5d4003b8939"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Reasoning Distiller Designer directive prioritizes explicit contracts, primitive boundaries, state/lifecycle models, failure semantics, and conformance criteria and instructs design work not to infer or exercise project authority."},"id":"pems:proposition:c0bf0280dc6712beffb0b7ab","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:49983005fb761f5f027888eb"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The admission transaction pressure test exercises exact-base guarded reused-record updates and explicit failure cases rather than mutating a live project Canon."},"id":"pems:proposition:c1c94ebd71528a54e3c81385","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:244fd27a8bca50c055c65717"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The uncertainty-import validator deterministically replays the additive RGP/1 uncertainty-to-PEMS compatibility profile."},"id":"pems:proposition:c2bef8f1c8fe2d03329346dc","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:bea35ff87e7c1aecc9cf8f03"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The v2 admission executor extends the transaction shape with exact guarded updates to reused records and delegates core transaction mechanics to the shared admission implementation."},"id":"pems:proposition:c38c0133d6875b67cad1e11f","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:2ec23e2db7887ba15ca4729c"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The invocation-result schema distinguishes successful immutable-submission results from explicit failure results under reasoning-distiller-invocation-result/1."},"id":"pems:proposition:c56b4b7f4632f12fbba9730d","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:3a1d0265c40c7ac70d4585e2"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Knowledge Systems Architect directive assigns generic representation, schema, backend-interface, validation, migration, compatibility, and package-boundary work while excluding project semantic admission and project-authority assignment."},"id":"pems:proposition:d44f87579c505fe2d472785a","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:03985c9760413e9ddc9f33a6"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The RGP validator deterministically validates both raw rgp/1 graphs and submission envelopes, including record/relation vocabulary, provenance shape, premise references/cycles, and structural invariants."},"id":"pems:proposition:d6737b69d4c78195e5d8e6aa","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:f247f491c9f79319dcec8994"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Project Knowledge Steward directive assigns project-scoped semantic identity, provenance sufficiency, conflict/supersession/lifecycle, guarded-update, and admission-transaction decisions only within authority granted by the consuming project."},"id":"pems:proposition:d9893bd87ae17e03c8105a32","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:ae29b365fc8dbf7615b205c7"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Distiller directive requires compact durable engineering propositions from observable evidence rather than hidden reasoning, limits record/relation vocabularies, and requires primary provenance for non-derived observations."},"id"